Aim: To implement image cropping, copying, and pasting using OpenCV to select and manipulate a region of interest (ROI) from a source image.
Observation:
- ROI selects a specific rectangular portion of the original image.
- Cropping extracts the selected region.
- The cropped region can be copied and pasted into another image or another location in the same image.
- The selected coordinates determine the size and position of the ROI.
Result: The region of interest was successfully selected, cropped, copied, and pasted using OpenCV
